820 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Indexing Pipeline: The set of processes that is employed to create the knowledge base for RAG applications. It is a non real-time pipeline that updates the knowledge base at periodic intervals.) /E (Indexing Pipeline: The set of processes that is employed to create the knowledge base for RAG applications. It is a non real-time pipeline that updates the knowledge base at periodic intervals.) /Alt () /Pg 15 0 R /K [3 ] >> endobj
821 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Source Systems: The original locations where the data that is desired for the RAG application is stored. These can be data lakes, file systems, CMSs, SQL & NoSQL databases, 3rd party data stores etc.) /E (Source Systems: The original locations where the data that is desired for the RAG application is stored. These can be data lakes, file systems, CMSs, SQL & NoSQL databases, 3rd party data stores etc.) /Alt () /Pg 15 0 R /K [4 ] >> endobj
822 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Data Loading: The first step of the indexing pipeline that connects to source systems to extract and parse files for data to be used in the RAG knowledge base.) /E (Data Loading: The first step of the indexing pipeline that connects to source systems to extract and parse files for data to be used in the RAG knowledge base.) /Alt () /Pg 15 0 R /K [5 ] >> endobj
823 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Metadata: A common way of defining metadata is data about dataŽ. Metadata describes other data. It can provide information like a description of the data, time of creation, author, etc. While metadata is useful for managing and organising data, in the context of RAG, metadata enhances the search-ability of data.) /E (Metadata: A common way of defining metadata is data about dataŽ. Metadata describes other data. It can provide information like a description of the data, time of creation, author, etc. While metadata is useful for managing and organising data, in the context of RAG, metadata enhances the search-ability of data.) /Alt () /Pg 15 0 R /K [6 ] >> endobj
