971 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Evaluation Metrics: Quantitative measures used to evaluate the performance of retrieval & generation and overall RAG system.) /E (Evaluation Metrics: Quantitative measures used to evaluate the performance of retrieval & generation and overall RAG system.) /Alt () /Pg 29 0 R /K [3 ] >> endobj
972 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Accuracy: The proportion of correct predictions \(both true positives and true negatives\) among the total number of cases examined. Even though accuracy is a simple, intuitive metric, it is not the primary metric for retrieval. In a large knowledge base, majority of documents are usually irrelevant to any given query, which can lead to misleadingly high accuracy scores. It does not consider ranking of the retrieved results.) /E (Accuracy: The proportion of correct predictions \(both true positives and true negatives\) among the total number of cases examined. Even though accuracy is a simple, intuitive metric, it is not the primary metric for retrieval. In a large knowledge base, majority of documents are usually irrelevant to any given query, which can lead to misleadingly high accuracy scores. It does not consider ranking of the retrieved results.) /Alt () /Pg 29 0 R /K [4 ] >> endobj
973 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Precision: It measures the proportion of retrieved documents that are relevant to the user query. It answers the question, Of all the documents that were retrieved, how many were actually relevant?Ž) /E (Precision: It measures the proportion of retrieved documents that are relevant to the user query. It answers the question, Of all the documents that were retrieved, how many were actually relevant?Ž) /Alt () /Pg 29 0 R /K [5 ] >> endobj
974 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Precision@k: A variation of precision that measures the proportion of relevant documents amongst the top k retrieved results. It is particularly important because it focusses on the top results rather than all the retrieved documents.) /E (Precision@k: A variation of precision that measures the proportion of relevant documents amongst the top k retrieved results. It is particularly important because it focusses on the top results rather than all the retrieved documents.) /Alt () /Pg 29 0 R /K [6 ] >> endobj
975 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Recall: It measures the proportion of the relevant documents retrieved from all the relevant documents in the corpus. It answers the question, Of all the relevant documents, how many were actually retrieved?Ž. Like precision, recall also doesnt consider the ranking of the retrieved documents. It can also be misleading as retrieving all documents in the knowledge base will result in a perfect recall value.) /E (Recall: It measures the proportion of the relevant documents retrieved from all the relevant documents in the corpus. It answers the question, Of all the relevant documents, how many were actually retrieved?Ž. Like precision, recall also doesnt consider the ranking of the retrieved documents. It can also be misleading as retrieving all documents in the knowledge base will result in a perfect recall value.) /Alt () /Pg 29 0 R /K [7 ] >> endobj
976 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (F1-score: The harmonic mean of precision and recall. It provides a single metric that balances both the quality and coverage of the retriever. ) /E (F1-score: The harmonic mean of precision and recall. It provides a single metric that balances both the quality and coverage of the retriever. ) /Alt () /Pg 29 0 R /K [8 ] >> endobj
