1004 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Answer Faithfulness: A measure of the extent to which the response is factually grounded in the retrieved context. Faithfulness ensures that the facts in the response do not contradict the context and can be traced back to the source. It also ensures that the LLM is not hallucinating. Faithfulness first identifies the number of claimsŽ made in the response and calculates the proportion of those claimsŽ present in the context.) /E (Answer Faithfulness: A measure of the extent to which the response is factually grounded in the retrieved context. Faithfulness ensures that the facts in the response do not contradict the context and can be traced back to the source. It also ensures that the LLM is not hallucinating. Faithfulness first identifies the number of claimsŽ made in the response and calculates the proportion of those claimsŽ present in the context.) /Alt () /Pg 32 0 R /K [3 ] >> endobj
1005 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Hallucination Rate: Calculate the proportion of generated claims in the response that are not present in the retrieved context) /E (Hallucination Rate: Calculate the proportion of generated claims in the response that are not present in the retrieved context) /Alt () /Pg 32 0 R /K [4 ] >> endobj
1006 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Coverage: Measures the number of relevant claims in the context and calculates the proportion of relevant claims present in the generated response. This measures how much of the relevant information from the retrieved passages is included in the generated answer.) /E (Coverage: Measures the number of relevant claims in the context and calculates the proportion of relevant claims present in the generated response. This measures how much of the relevant information from the retrieved passages is included in the generated answer.) /Alt () /Pg 32 0 R /K [5 ] >> endobj
1007 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Answer Relevance: Measure of the extent to which the response is relevant to the query. This metric focusses on key aspects such as systems ability to comprehend the query, response being pertinent to the query and the completeness of the response. ) /E (Answer Relevance: Measure of the extent to which the response is relevant to the query. This metric focusses on key aspects such as systems ability to comprehend the query, response being pertinent to the query and the completeness of the response. ) /Alt () /Pg 32 0 R /K [6 ] >> endobj
1008 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Ground truth: Information that is known to be real or true. In RAG, and Generative AI domain in general, Ground Truth is a prepared set of Prompt-Context-Response or Question-Context-Response example, akin to labelled data in Supervised Machine Learning parlance. Ground truth data that is created for your knowledge base can be used for evaluation of your RAG system. ) /E (Ground truth: Information that is known to be real or true. In RAG, and Generative AI domain in general, Ground Truth is a prepared set of Prompt-Context-Response or Question-Context-Response example, akin to labelled data in Supervised Machine Learning parlance. Ground truth data that is created for your knowledge base can be used for evaluation of your RAG system. ) /Alt () /Pg 32 0 R /K [7 ] >> endobj
1009 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Human Evaluation: A subject matter expert looking at the documents and determines the relevance and accuracy of the outputs.) /E (Human Evaluation: A subject matter expert looking at the documents and determines the relevance and accuracy of the outputs.) /Alt () /Pg 32 0 R /K [8 ] >> endobj
