1094 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H4 /T (Hybrid Retrieval: Hybrid retrieval strategy is an essential component of production-grade RAG systems. It involves combining retrieval methods for improved retrieval accuracy. This can mean simply using a keyword-based search along with semantic similarity. It can also mean combining all sparse embedding, dense embedding vector and knowledge graph-based search. ) /E (Hybrid Retrieval: Hybrid retrieval strategy is an essential component of production-grade RAG systems. It involves combining retrieval methods for improved retrieval accuracy. This can mean simply using a keyword-based search along with semantic similarity. It can also mean combining all sparse embedding, dense embedding vector and knowledge graph-based search. ) /Alt () /Pg 40 0 R /K [4 ] >> endobj
1095 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H4 /T (Iterative Retrieval: In this approach the retrieval happens n number of times and the generated response is used to further retrieve documents each time.) /E (Iterative Retrieval: In this approach the retrieval happens n number of times and the generated response is used to further retrieve documents each time.) /Alt () /Pg 40 0 R /K [5 ] >> endobj
1096 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H4 /T (Recursive Retrieval: This approach improves upon the iterative approach by transforming the retrieval query after each generation.) /E (Recursive Retrieval: This approach improves upon the iterative approach by transforming the retrieval query after each generation.) /Alt () /Pg 40 0 R /K [6 ] >> endobj
1097 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H4 /T (Adaptive Retrieval: This is a more intelligent approach where an LLM determines the most appropriate moment and the most appropriate content for retrieval.) /E (Adaptive Retrieval: This is a more intelligent approach where an LLM determines the most appropriate moment and the most appropriate content for retrieval.) /Alt () /Pg 40 0 R /K [7 ] >> endobj
