1414 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Incoherent Summarisation: Generating inconsistent or disjointed summaries from multiple retrieved documents, leading to poor user experience.) /E (Incoherent Summarisation: Generating inconsistent or disjointed summaries from multiple retrieved documents, leading to poor user experience.) /Alt () /Pg 57 0 R /K [4 ] >> endobj
1415 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Over-Generation: Generating overly verbose or redundant responses based on retrieved data that fails to condense the key points effectively.) /E (Over-Generation: Generating overly verbose or redundant responses based on retrieved data that fails to condense the key points effectively.) /Alt () /Pg 57 0 R /K [5 ] >> endobj
1416 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Inconsistent Modal Alignment: Challenges integrating multimodal data \(e.g., text, images, videos\) where retrieved content across different modalities may not be aligned properly, affecting the quality of the generated response.) /E (Inconsistent Modal Alignment: Challenges integrating multimodal data \(e.g., text, images, videos\) where retrieved content across different modalities may not be aligned properly, affecting the quality of the generated response.) /Alt () /Pg 57 0 R /K [6 ] >> endobj
1417 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Data Silos: When knowledge is fragmented across multiple sources or platforms, retrieval becomes challenging due to inconsistent indexing or lack of interoperability between knowledge bases.) /E (Data Silos: When knowledge is fragmented across multiple sources or platforms, retrieval becomes challenging due to inconsistent indexing or lack of interoperability between knowledge bases.) /Alt () /Pg 57 0 R /K [7 ] >> endobj
1418 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Processing Large-Scale Data: Difficulty in maintaining high throughput and low latency as the amount of indexed data grows.) /E (Processing Large-Scale Data: Difficulty in maintaining high throughput and low latency as the amount of indexed data grows.) /Alt () /Pg 57 0 R /K [8 ] >> endobj
1419 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H3 /T (Multi-Agent Coordination: When multiple agents are used for task orchestration \(as in agentic RAG\), coordination among agents can become complex and resource-heavy, impacting system efficiency.) /E (Multi-Agent Coordination: When multiple agents are used for task orchestration \(as in agentic RAG\), coordination among agents can become complex and resource-heavy, impacting system efficiency.) /Alt () /Pg 57 0 R /K [9 ] >> endobj
